WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.652 --> 00:00:06.694
It is almost Christmas.

2
00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:10.096
Today the Smith family is going to get their Christmas tree.

3
00:00:10.116 --> 00:00:13.837
"Come on, Jay and Sarah.

4
00:00:14.257 --> 00:00:16.058
Let's get going," says Dad.

5
00:00:16.078 --> 00:00:18.199
"Where are we going, Dad?"

6
00:00:18.619 --> 00:00:19.179
asks Jay.

7
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.161
"We're going to the Christmas tree farm."

8
00:00:23.201 --> 00:00:24.742
Jay and Sarah are excited.

9
00:00:24.762 --> 00:00:26.422
"All right!"

10
00:00:26.763 --> 00:00:27.283
they cheer.

11
00:00:28.023 --> 00:00:32.137
When the Smith family arrives at the tree farm, they see thousands of Christmas trees.

12
00:00:34.218 --> 00:00:35.759
"Look at all the trees.

13
00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:39.201
They are planted in straight rows," says Sarah.

14
00:00:40.102 --> 00:00:43.223
"They have many kinds of Christmas trees," Dad says.

15
00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:47.066
"Yes," says Mom, "those are white pines.

16
00:00:47.686 --> 00:00:49.547
And these are spruce trees."

17
00:00:50.468 --> 00:00:51.828
Picking a tree is not easy.

18
00:00:52.709 --> 00:00:53.970
Some trees are too small.

19
00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.751
Some trees are too big.

20
00:00:56.431 --> 00:00:57.672
Some trees are not straight.

21
00:00:59.576 --> 00:01:01.017
"How about this tree?"

22
00:01:01.457 --> 00:01:02.517
says Jay, pointing.

23
00:01:02.537 --> 00:01:05.658
"It's too thin, Jay," Dad says.

24
00:01:05.678 --> 00:01:07.799
"What about that tree?"

25
00:01:08.019 --> 00:01:08.800
suggests Sarah.

26
00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:09.960
Mom disagrees.

27
00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.261
"It's too twisty, Sarah."

28
00:01:13.602 --> 00:01:15.662
Then Mom finds a tall, straight tree.

29
00:01:15.682 --> 00:01:17.403
"I like that tree.

30
00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:19.644
It is a perfect Christmas tree."

31
00:01:19.664 --> 00:01:23.986
"Wow! I like it too," says Jay.

32
00:01:24.686 --> 00:01:26.807
"It's beautiful," says Sarah.

33
00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:27.807
Dad agrees.

34
00:01:27.827 --> 00:01:29.288
"Let's cut it down."

35
00:01:29.592 --> 00:01:32.254
With a chain saw, he cuts through the trunk of the tree.

36
00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:37.517
"Stay back, Jay.

37
00:01:37.918 --> 00:01:39.819
It's going to fall," warns Mom.

38
00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:46.283
Mom and Dad go to pay for the tree, and Sarah and Jay enjoy a hot cup of

39
00:01:46.383 --> 00:01:47.024
apple cider.

40
00:01:47.524 --> 00:01:49.886
The tree farm makes delicious hot apple cider.

41
00:01:50.166 --> 00:01:51.587
Soon, it is time to go.

42
00:01:51.607 --> 00:01:52.988
"Thank you very much.

43
00:01:53.268 --> 00:01:55.870
Enjoy your tree," says the man at the tree farm.

44
00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:59.112
"Merry Christmas," the Smiths say.

45
00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.921
In the parking lot, they tie their new Christmas tree to the roof of the car.

46
00:02:04.741 --> 00:02:05.742
Then they drive home.

47
00:02:06.402 --> 00:02:08.382
Cutting down the tree is only half the fun.

48
00:02:08.722 --> 00:02:10.983
When they get home, it is time to decorate it.

49
00:02:11.003 --> 00:02:14.724
"Brush the snow off the tree," says Mom.

50
00:02:14.744 --> 00:02:17.765
"I'll get the Christmas tree stand," says Dad.

51
00:02:18.345 --> 00:02:20.186
Dad puts the tree into the stand.

52
00:02:21.146 --> 00:02:23.226
Without the stand, the tree cannot stand up.

53
00:02:24.287 --> 00:02:26.067
"Now we can decorate the tree."

54
00:02:26.087 --> 00:02:30.056
"First we must put the lights on," says Mom.

55
00:02:30.657 --> 00:02:33.098
Sarah makes sure that every lightbulb works.

56
00:02:33.599 --> 00:02:35.500
Dad and Jay put the lights on the tree.

57
00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.181
"Look at this one.

58
00:02:37.702 --> 00:02:39.483
It's pretty," says Sarah.

59
00:02:40.303 --> 00:02:43.345
"The tin soldiers are my favorite," says Jay.

60
00:02:43.365 --> 00:02:48.909
"Now, Jay and Sarah," says Mom, "you can put some tinsel on the tree."

61
00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.752
When they are done, Sarah is pleased.

62
00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:56.334
"Wow, it looks beautiful."

63
00:02:56.774 --> 00:02:57.915
The tree is almost finished.

64
00:02:58.515 --> 00:03:00.741
It looks great, but there is one thing missing.

65
00:03:00.761 --> 00:03:02.483
"The star!"

66
00:03:02.763 --> 00:03:03.344
says Mom.

67
00:03:04.465 --> 00:03:07.167
No Christmas tree is complete without a star on top.

68
00:03:08.148 --> 00:03:12.112
Dad lifts Jay up so that he can place the star on the top of the tree.

69
00:03:12.132 --> 00:03:14.474
"Perfect!" says Mom.

70
00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:18.738
"This is the greatest Christmas tree ever," says Sarah.

71
00:03:19.619 --> 00:03:20.500
And everyone agrees!
